Goal:
Build strong cybersecurity fundamentals alongside Fernstudium.
No rush to job. Focus on deep understanding and long-term skill.

Principles:
- Understand systems, not just tools
- Build first → use tools later
- No rushing, no surface-level learning
- Consistency > speed

Phase 1 (Current):
- Build core systems (server, attacker, detection)
- Understand networking, logs, behavior
- Be able to explain everything clearly

Phase 2:
- Expand systems (better detection, simulation, logging)
- Rebuild parts from scratch (gain fluency)
- Remove “magic” feeling

Phase 3:
- Introduce Virtual Machine (Kali Linux)
- Use real tools (nmap, hydra, etc.)
- Map tools → concepts already learned

Phase 4:
- TryHackMe / labs
- Apply knowledge in real scenarios
- Focus on pattern recognition

Focus Direction:
Balanced, but leaning toward:
- analysis
- detection
- system understanding

Not optimizing for:
- fast job entry
- memorization
- shortcuts